{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1f685894-e3cd-4970-b02f-ca9262883724","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc5eb7bbef65b70d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-swy7tzsf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md","content":"# AMD Instinct validation campaign: vLLM ROCm serving parity and go/no-go scope\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: whether vLLM serving on AMD\nInstinct accelerators achieves functional and performance parity with the\nproductized CUDA builds for the platform's supported model set. It runs a\nvalidation campaign on physical AMD GPU hardware, records per-model functional\nand performance results, and produces the go/no-go recommendation that\ndetermines the scope of the ROCm serving runtime productization work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the campaign plan for the supported model set: per-model functional\n  checks and performance measurements (throughput and latency) against the CUDA\n  baseline, on single- and multi-GPU serving configurations where applicable.\n- Secure access to dedicated AMD Instinct nodes (procurement or partner-lab\n  access) — access itself is an externally-controlled precondition tracked as a\n  risk, not a deliverable condition.\n- Execute the campaign using upstream vLLM ROCm runtime builds on the supported\n  model set.\n- Record functional parity results (pass/fail per model) and performance parity\n  data (per-model measurements versus CUDA baseline).\n- Produce the go/no-go report: the per-model list cleared for productization,\n  gaps found, and the recommended productization scope.\n- Track upstream ROCm image availability for the models and configurations\n  under test.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A validation report exists covering every model in the supported model set,\n  with functional pass/fail results and performance measurements recorded from\n  execution on physical AMD Instinct hardware.\n- Each model's functional result is a defined pass/fail against the CUDA\n  baseline behavior for the same serving configuration.\n- Performance data (throughput and latency) is captured per model and compared\n  against the CUDA baseline in the report.\n- The report states a per-model go/no-go recommendation and an overall\n  recommended productization scope, such that the serving runtime\n  productization work can proceed on a defined model list.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: A validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware\n  establishes functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the\n  supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Hardware access is unresolved (procurement or partner-lab); it is externally\n  controlled and may gate campaign start timing.\n- Upstream ROCm runtime image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the\n  upstream communities; image availability for specific models or\n  configurations may lag.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33122,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3822dea5e536a0c","agent_id":"ac819e8af2b356d4b","session_id":"8431d8a2-78f2-40cd-ac08-9c04fa95fff4","uuid":"59a2a1cc-ff85-4e63-9387-59739f4bb645","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:21:43.198Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
