t mode.\n- The documented supported model list for the ROCm runtime matches exactly the\n  models cleared by the validation campaign's go/no-go report.\n- Existing CUDA vLLM runtime builds and their ServingRuntime definitions are\n  unchanged by this work.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)**: A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n  models the validation campaign clears.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Upstream ROCm runtime image release cadence is controlled by AMD and may not\n  align with platform release trains; mitigation is pinning to validated image\n  versions and rebuilding as needed.\n- The epic's scope (which models are covered) is determined by the validation\n  campaign outcome; if no model clears, this epic is removed and parity gaps\n  are reported upstream instead.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33872,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3822dea5e536a0c","agent_id":"ac819e8af2b356d4b","session_id":"8431d8a2-78f2-40cd-ac08-9c04fa95fff4","uuid":"1cc52eb9-f150-492c-aab6-04b08f956bf9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.645Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
