ods are identified and\n  recorded for inclusion in product documentation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)** (partial): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single-\n  and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue — the Training Operator / job\n  execution portion. The amd.com/gpu quota handling portion is covered by the\n  Kueue quota configuration work.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Requires access to AMD Instinct nodes for validation; shared with the\n  serving validation campaign (coordination risk, not a dependency).\n- Relies on upstream PyTorch ROCm image/wheel availability for the tested\n  PyTorch versions.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34575,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3822dea5e536a0c","agent_id":"ac819e8af2b356d4b","session_id":"8431d8a2-78f2-40cd-ac08-9c04fa95fff4","uuid":"f39d20e3-0a2d-47c4-9325-b93f600528bc","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:22:02.266Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
