anifests with\n  usage documentation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)** (partial): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single-\n  and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling —\n  the Kueue quota/admission portion. The PyTorchJob execution portion is\n  covered by the Training Operator ROCm training work.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Requires AMD Instinct nodes with AMD GPU resource discovery for end-to-end\n  validation; shared with the other AMD validation work (coordination risk,\n  not a dependency).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35268,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3822dea5e536a0c","agent_id":"ac819e8af2b356d4b","session_id":"8431d8a2-78f2-40cd-ac08-9c04fa95fff4","uuid":"0df28aeb-d796-4445-b02f-e8a91a24baf1","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:22:11.373Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
