y decisions recorded in the summary** (`artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-decomposition.md`): tiered delivery (Tier 1 = E001/E003/E004 independent value; Tier 2 = E002 gated by campaign outcome and upstream ROCm image cadence); health warnings for missing strategy sections (no Impacted Teams, Dependencies, Given/When/Then ACs, NFRs — teams derived from architecture-context owners), the two open questions as external risks, and shared-hardware coordination between serving and training validation. Upstream ROCm cadence was modeled as a precondition/risk rather than an upstream-PR epic (Rule 21 doesn't apply — we consume AMD's releases, we don't contribute to them). Each epic also has its own `-ai-signals.md` rationale file; E001 uses the 5 investigation signals (notably `cluster_hardware_dependence=-2` since the gating question requires physical AMD GPUs), the rest use the 9 implementation signals with `architecture_claims=1` citing the corroborating `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/` files."}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45380,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3822dea5e536a0c","agent_id":"ac819e8af2b356d4b","session_id":"8431d8a2-78f2-40cd-ac08-9c04fa95fff4","uuid":"3dc9f765-6564-445d-bb91-17869e6687f6","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:23:54.627Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
