{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaac912100593905","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for campaign-cleared models\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: Productize only the model subset the validation campaign clears;\n15\t    if no model clears, remove this epic and report parity gaps upstream instead of\n16\t    shipping a supported ROCm runtime.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 4\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for campaign-cleared models\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic delivers a supported, productized vLLM ROCm serving runtime image and\n39\tits serving runtime definition, covering the models cleared by the AMD Instinct\n40\tvalidation campaign. It turns the validated upstream ROCm capability into a\n41\tplatform-shipped runtime that deploys under KServe InferenceServices alongside\n42\tthe existing CUDA builds.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Build the vLLM ROCm runtime image variant from the upstream ROCm base images,\n47\t  through the existing runtime image build and release pipeline used for\n48\t  productized runtimes.\n49\t- Publish the ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime definition for the ROCm\n50\t  vLLM runtime so it can be selected for InferenceService deployment.\n51\t- Restrict the declared supported model list to the models cleared by the\n52\t  validation campaign's go/no-go report.\n53\t- Verify KServe compatibility: InferenceServices using the ROCm runtime deploy\n54\t  and reach Ready (including raw deployment mode, the recommended path for\n55\t  disconnected environments).\n56\t- Keep the existing CUDA (NVIDIA) vLLM builds unaffected — the ROCm runtime is\n57\t  additive, not a replacement.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- A vLLM ROCm runtime image builds and releases green through the existing\n62\t  runtime image pipeline, with the image published for the platform release.\n63\t- A ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime definition for the ROCm vLLM runtime\n64\t  is published and deployable.\n65\t- An InferenceService using the ROCm vLLM runtime for a cleared model deploys\n66\t  successfully and reaches Ready, including in raw deployment mode.\n67\t- The documented supported model list for the ROCm runtime matches exactly the\n68\t  models cleared by the validation campaign's go/no-go report.\n69\t- Existing CUDA vLLM runtime builds and their ServingRuntime definitions are\n70\t  unchanged by this work.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n75\t  models the validation campaign clears.\n76\t\n77\t## Risks / Notes\n78\t\n79\t- Upstream ROCm runtime image release cadence is controlled by AMD and may not\n80\t  align with platform release trains; mitigation is pinning to validated image\n81\t  versions and rebuilding as needed.\n82\t- The epic's scope (which models are covered) is determined by the validation\n83\t  campaign outcome; if no model clears, this epic is removed and parity gaps\n84\t  are reported upstream instead.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1e4160c1c5d645b","agent_id":"a2a11fda56fb9b166","session_id":"8431d8a2-78f2-40cd-ac08-9c04fa95fff4","uuid":"9bea3b4