{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7fa2878a0d5d972","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic enables PyTorch training on AMD Instinct accelerators using the\n34\tTraining Operator: PyTorchJobs running ROCm PyTorch training images execute\n35\tcorrectly on AMD GPU nodes for both single-GPU and multi-GPU (including\n36\tmulti-node) job topologies, admitted through Kueue workload queueing.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Enable and validate PyTorchJob execution with ROCm PyTorch training images\n41\t  on AMD Instinct worker nodes, for single-GPU and multi-GPU distributed\n42\t  topologies.\n43\t- Verify job specs request AMD GPU resources (amd.com/gpu) correctly for the\n44\t  job topology, including gang-scheduled multi-node jobs.\n45\t- Validate that PyTorchJobs requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted through Kueue\n46\t  queueing and run to completion (the quota configuration itself is delivered\n47\t  by the Kueue quota handling work; this epic validates training jobs against\n48\t  it as an acceptance gate).\n49\t- Document any Training Operator changes or configuration needed for ROCm\n50\t  worker nodes (driver/runtime prerequisites on the job pods).\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob using a ROCm PyTorch training image runs to\n55\t  completion on an AMD Instinct node with correct training results.\n56\t- A multi-GPU (and multi-node, where topology permits) PyTorchJob using ROCm\n57\t  PyTorch training images runs to completion with distributed training\n58\t  functioning correctly across GPUs.\n59\t- PyTorchJobs requesting amd.com/gpu resources are admitted through Kueue\n60\t  queueing and execute on AMD GPU nodes.\n61\t- Any driver/runtime prerequisites for ROCm job pods are identified and\n62\t  recorded for inclusion in product documentation.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- **HLR-3 (P1)** (partial): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single-\n67\t  and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue — the Training Operator / job\n68\t  execution portion. The amd.com/gpu quota handling portion is covered by the\n69\t  Kueue quota configuration work.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks / Notes\n72\t\n73\t- Requires access to AMD Instinct nodes for validation; shared with the\n74\t  serving validation campaign (coordination risk, not a dependency).\n75\t- Relies on upstream PyTorch ROCm image/wheel availability for the tested\n76\t  PyTorch versions.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1e4160c1c5d645b","agent_id":"a2a11fda56fb9b166","session_id":"8431d8a2-78f2-40cd-ac08-9c04fa95fff4","uuid":"e48048e1-5dc6-46c4-b625-3b4e91c05646","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:31:06.853Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7fa2878a0d5d972","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
