{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d906d5909a07b5d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for ROCm workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for ROCm workloads\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers amd.com/gpu quota handling in the platform's Kueue-based\n34\tdistributed workloads stack, so that workloads requesting AMD GPU resources are\n35\tadmitted with correct quota accounting — queued when quota is exhausted,\n36\tadmitted when capacity is available, with all-or-nothing gang semantics for\n37\tmulti-pod jobs.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Define the Kueue resource flavor and ClusterQueue/LocalQueue configuration\n42\t  covering the amd.com/gpu resource, so AMD GPU capacity is quota-managed like\n43\t  existing accelerator resources.\n44\t- Implement or configure quota accounting for amd.com/gpu requests in\n45\t  workload admission (covering any code or configuration gap between Kueue's\n46\t  quota model and AMD GPU resource discovery on Instinct nodes).\n47\t- Validate admission behavior: workloads requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted\n48\t  when quota is available, held pending when quota is exhausted, and\n49\t  multi-pod workloads are admitted all-or-nothing.\n50\t- Deliver the quota configuration as deployable, documented manifests for\n51\t  clusters with AMD GPU nodes.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A workload requesting amd.com/gpu is admitted through Kueue when quota is\n56\t  available and remains pending (not partially admitted) when quota is\n57\t  exhausted.\n58\t- Multi-pod workloads requesting amd.com/gpu are admitted with all-or-nothing\n59\t  semantics.\n60\t- Quota accounting for amd.com/gpu is correct: admitted usage counts against\n61\t  the configured ClusterQueue quota and is released when workloads finish.\n62\t- The quota configuration is delivered as versioned, deployable manifests with\n63\t  usage documentation.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- **HLR-3 (P1)** (partial): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single-\n68\t  and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling —\n69\t  the Kueue quota/admission portion. The PyTorchJob execution portion is\n70\t  covered by the Training Operator ROCm training work.\n71\t\n72\t## Risks / Notes\n73\t\n74\t- Requires AMD Instinct nodes with AMD GPU resource discovery for end-to-end\n75\t  validation; shared with the other AMD validation work (coordination risk,\n76\t  not a dependency).\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1e4160c1c5d645b","agent_id":"a2a11fda56fb9b166","session_id":"8431d8a2-78f2-40cd-ac08-9c04fa95fff4","uuid":"2d29eb1a-b8d4-4576-973b-4254e4f97a65","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:31:07.484Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d906d5909a07b5d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
